Z||000000||Return of Fiero||12-24-2001||03:23 AM||||I'm sure that one of my fans will say im ignorent due to the fact that i dont use the spelling corection supplied, though I know my spelling is lees than adiquit, but this isnt about personal ignorence.<P>I saw somthing today that sort of bothered me, it was a racial thread written on a public bench. The first thing that was written was "Blacks suck." a bit shocked at the boldness of writing such a thing. Then quickly realizing the had not signed there "master peice," showed how cowardly they were.<P>The next line down read "You only show your ignorence by writing such trash." An admireable contribution to the ledger, as it brought some sort of justice to me knowing someone was nice enough to needlessly defend such an assinine writing.<P>The line following it was of the first autor, and showed up 2 days later. "Your trash." Obviously the same idiot, as it was equaly ignorent.<P>Next day, it read one line down "I'm not white trash, I'm white class."<P>The last line that was writen was later that day, and it was short and simple. "F@#$ YOU!"<P>Now the only reason I wrote this was it really disturbs me that people still think in this fasion, and feel it is there right to tear someone down, not for what they do personaly, but for who they are as a culture. In this, im saying people are torn on for their religion, or race, or any other general clasifacation they are, and are never given the chance to show who. The narrow minded veiw that this ignorent autor showed it something I saw alot of as a taxi driver, and it bothers me. If i didnt depend on the fair and the tip, i would have liked to have pulled over and told them i thing or two. Do we still live in such a world were people see color, or race, and never other people. I would like to think not, but more and more, i see it everyday. Why do we as people do this to ourselves, and also, let this go on? sorry, all, im just feeling really bad about this, because a person had the balls to walk by a nice lady i know, who works for salvation army, saying, "I'm not giving money this time, theres a nig# standing there." It made me sick, and pissed. if the cop wasnt there, i dont think i would have controled myself.<P>Sorry about the lenght, i just needed to spout off, and hoped someone would see my point.<P>Myke<BR>BTW, if you were wondering, my ancestrey is canadian french, perishin french, swiss, and english.||||reg||9
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||12-24-2001||08:12 AM||||Hey Myke!<BR>That is totally unacceptable...<BR>If it is written down, it gets washed or painted...<BR>But when someone says something like that, speak up, especially if a cop is nearby...<BR>I would of said something like "With an attitude like that, who wants your money?"<BR>or "So you only gave to the white people of New York?"<BR>If they come back with "FREEDOM OF SPEACH", say it doesn't mean "FREEDOM TO HATE"...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
